    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d274">

                <pb facs="0246" n="240" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102 Tientsin/497</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Adviser on Political Relations</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornbeck</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-08-29">August 29, 1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Under instruction from the Secretary, I informed Mr. Mallet today that the
                    Department perceived and felt no objection to the procedure on the part of the
                    British Ambassador in Tokyo indicated in the communication from the British
                    Embassy of August 28, here attached.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d274-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stanley K.
                    Hornbeck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
